cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ReasonedOps in research, teaching, demos, or derived work, please cite this software."
title: "ReasonedOps"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Cheng"
    given-names: "Gigi"
version: "1.4.3"
date-released: 2026-08-21
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/gigichengnc/reasoned-ops"
url: "https://github.com/gigichengnc/reasoned-ops"
abstract: >-
  ReasonedOps originated from the author's participation in HKMU Hackathon 2026 and
  evolved into an evidence-aware service-operations research/software prototype organised
  around Operate, Audit, and Evaluate. Operate uses a transparent deterministic rule-based
  routing baseline rather than claiming a trained NLP model. Audit preserves machine and
  human decision history separately from observed outcomes. Evaluate first checks whether
  a comparison and method are supportable before reporting adjusted evidence, and its
  synthetic validity benchmark includes an explicit unmeasured-confounding blind spot in
  which observed-data checks can pass while the adjusted answer is materially wrong.
  Regression/ANCOVA is one method inside Evaluate rather than the project identity. Current
  quantitative evidence is synthetic or hand-authored development evidence and does not
  establish real-world service improvement, causal effects, private-data pilot approval,
  or production readiness.
keywords:
  - "service operations"
  - "human-in-the-loop"
  - "evidence-aware evaluation"
  - "ANCOVA"
  - "regression"
  - "offline policy evaluation"
  - "longitudinal analysis"
  - "data governance"
  - "responsible AI"
